"""Wf-408-A3 — pre-flight 2 FAIL fixes + launcher --wave 1/2/3 alias regression-guard.

Per the Wf-407-A3 baseline (PRESERVED across Wf-408-A3) two pre-flight FAILs
needed CPU-only closure and one launcher needed a `--wave` CLI extension.
This test module is the regression-guard surface — it asserts each fix
remains in place across future wave activity.

Surface coverage:

  * ``test_loi_status_header_present_in_4_files`` — every LOI draft
    carries the canonical ``TEMPLATE_NOT_NEEDED_FOR_TIER2`` marker on
    the ``**Status:**`` line (AGENTS.md §5.4 + §10 + 2026-09-30 user
    reinforcement). The 4 LOI drafts are:
      - wetlab_loi_rusanov_2025_platinai.md
      - wetlab_loi_pku_cisplatin_ic50.md
      - wetlab_loi_xiehe_nci60.md
      - wetlab_loi_ornl_protein_metal.md

  * ``test_loi_status_regex_accepts_tier2_marker`` — the gate regex in
    ``gate_loi_send_ready`` accepts the new marker (preserved Wf-405-A3
    fix). We pin via re.compile over the actual source string.

  * ``test_anchor_freshness_refresh_under_24h`` — the 6 refreshed anchor
    files (5 stale + wf269c_report.json per task brief) have mtime
    ``now - mtime <= 24h``. CPU-only stat() check.

  * ``test_launcher_accepts_wave_letters_and_all`` — the launcher
    ``--wave`` arg accepts the canonical ``A | B | C | all`` form.
    Verified via subprocess ``bash --dry-run --wave X`` exit code.

  * ``test_launcher_accepts_wave_1_2_3_aliases`` — the launcher
